<title>BRAZIL: RESEARCH ALERT - Telebras downgraded.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT - Telebras downgraded.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Morgan Stanley Dean Witter said it had downgraded Telebras to Outperform from Strong Buy and was maintaining its 12 month target price of $180 per ADS, which implied an upside potential of 14 percent from current levels.</p>
<p>-- Analyst Luiz Carvalho said he was maintaining his earnings estimates of $10.76 and $12.59 for 1997 and 1998, respectively.</p>
<p>-- Carvalho said that after the very strong performance in recent weeks, Telebras had now reached a valuation level that is closer to those of its Latin American and global peers.</p>
<p>-- Telebras preferred closed up 4.53 percent at 170.70 reais on the Sao Paulo exchange on Tuesday.</p>
<p>((-- Adrian Dickson, Sao Paulo newsroom 5511 248 5410))</p>
